====== Leetcode 206. Reverse Linked List =======
Step-by-step algorithm to reverse a linked list:

Step 1: Initialize a pointer pre to null.
This will store the previous node.

Step 2: Initialize a pointer head to the first node of the list.
(This is the current node.)

Step 3: Repeat the following steps while head is not null:

Sub-step 3a: Store the next node of head in a temporary pointer nxt.
(This prevents losing the rest of the list.)

Sub-step 3b: Change the next pointer of head to point to pre.
(This reverses the link.)

Sub-step 3c: Move pre to the current node (head).
(Now this node becomes the previous node.)

Sub-step 3d: Move head to nxt.
(Move to the next node in the original list.)

Step 4: When the loop ends, pre will point to the new head of the reversed list.

Step 5: Return pre.

Time Complexity:
Each node is visited once.
Time Complexity = O(n)

Space Complexity:
Only a few pointers are used.
Space Complexity = O(1)


         ---------------> Code <----------------
class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {
        ListNode pre=null;
        ListNode nxt=head;
        while(head!=null){
            nxt=head.next;
            head.next=pre;
            pre=head;
            head=nxt;
        }
        return pre;
    }
}
